WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.500
Indonesia is the world's largest archipelagic state with 17,508 islands spanning the equator.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Puncak Jaya in Papua rises to 4,884 meters with equatorial glaciers as Indonesia's highest point.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:17.000
Borobudur in Central Java is the largest Buddhist temple monument in the world, built in the 9th century.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.000
Indonesian Batik is recognized by UNESCO as Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.000
World-famous cuisine includes spicy Rendang from Minangkabau, fragrant Nasi Tumpeng, and Satay.

